.TH ZERODDS-XMLC 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-xmlc \- DDS-XML validator, deployment renderer, type lister
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-xmlc
.I command
.I file.xml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-xmlc
is a command-line front-end over the ZeroDDS DDS-XML parsers (OMG
DDS-XML 1.0). It parses a deployment file and reports; it never touches
the network.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate \fIFILE.xml\fR
Check well-formedness and parse every DDS-XML library (types, qos,
domain, participant, application). Print a one-line tally. Exit 1 on a
parse or validation error.
.TP
.B render \fIFILE.xml\fR
Print a structured deployment summary: domains and their topics,
participants and their publishers/subscribers with the data
writers/readers underneath.
.TP
.B types \fIFILE.xml\fR
List the
.B <types>
(XTypes) definitions, recursing into modules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-unknown
Leave out what the DDS-XML 1.0 schemas do not define (the elements and
attributes of another product's file) and list each omission with its path on
standard error. Without it the first such element is an error.
.TP
.B \-\-vendor\-forms
Read the forms other DDS products write (such as
.B <topic_filter>
as an element,
.BR qos_profile_ref ,
.BR <participant_qos> ,
IDL type names) and list each with its path on standard error. Without it the
first such form is an error that names the form DDS-XML 1.0 uses.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing to report.
.TP
.B 1
A library failed to parse.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong.
.TP
.B 3
A file could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a deployment file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
zerodds-xmlc validate deployment.xml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Render the deployment tree:
.PP
.RS
.nf
zerodds-xmlc render deployment.xml
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-admin (1),
.BR zerodds-idlc (1)
